.dev.vars

# Agent worktrees. Created inside the repo by the Agent tool with
# isolation: "worktree", removed when the agent finishes. They are gitlinks,
# not content — committing them (2026-08-06, feb4672) put ten dangling
# submodule pointers in a public repo that would break any fresh clone, and
# `git add -A` is what picked them up. Ignored so it cannot happen again.
.claude/worktrees/

# Session transcripts and health exports, whatever they are called. On
# 2026-08-08 `last_session.md`/`.rtf` (357 KB each, RTF, a full transcript) sat
# here untracked and UNIGNORED while the session ran `git add -A` three times.
# This repo is public and holds one person's health data. `verify.sh` also fails
# on a *tracked* file whose CONTENT looks like a transcript or an export, because
# ignoring a filename retires the instance and a content check retires the class.
last_session.*
*transcript*.md
*transcript*.rtf
*-export*.json
health-insights-export*.json
